        <mxCell id="safety" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=14;fillColor=#fff2f2;strokeColor=#cc0000;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#660000;" value="&lt;b&gt;⚠ The three safety rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Disable tools by default.&lt;/b&gt; Start with all tools off (VS Code turns on 118), and enable only what a task needs. Keep approvals on.&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;Be careful with .md files from public collections.&lt;/b&gt; Agents, skills, prompt files and instructions are instructions the model obeys. Read the raw file and its tools: list before using it.&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;Keep secrets out of the model&#39;s reach.&lt;/b&gt; .gitignore only keeps a file out of Git: an agent can still read .env and send it to a cloud model. Keep secrets outside the project folder, and block reading them in each harness.&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;More: local servers on the network, pickle files, pinned downloads, privacy, logs, credentials, and &quot;an example, not a product&quot; — see readme-safety.md&lt;/i&gt;" vertex="1">
